## Coverage Best Practices

### Test Organization
- Group tests by functionality
- Use descriptive test names
- Keep tests focused and single-purpose
- Use fixtures for common setup

### Coverage Analysis
- Review coverage reports regularly
- Focus on critical code paths first
- Don't chase 100% coverage blindly
- Ensure meaningful coverage, not just line count

### Maintenance
- Update tests when code changes
- Remove obsolete tests
- Refactor tests for better maintainability
- Keep test data and fixtures up-to-date

## Enforcement
Coverage standards are **MANDATORY** for all code changes. Coverage reports must be generated and reviewed before merging any code. Coverage thresholds must be maintained or improved with each change.
